text.section:
If the appropriate licensing authority determines that the settlement agent licensed by it or any of its other licensees has violated this chapter, or any regulation or order adopted thereunder, after notice and opportunity to be heard, the appropriate licensing authority may do one or more of the following:

Impose a civil penalty not exceeding $5,000 for each violation;


Revoke or suspend the applicable licenses;


Issue a restraining order requiring such person to cease and desist from engaging in such act or practice; or


Require restitution to be made by the person violating this chapter in the amount of any actual, direct financial loss.
